WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.466
(soft acoustic music)

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.330
- I'm just gonna tell you
a little bit about my mom.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.460
- I am going to tell you about my mom.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.460
- I was raised by my mom and my abuelita.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.040
So I like to say I was raised

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.620
in a space of matriarchal magic.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.770
- My dad, he just, he wasn't around,

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.870
so my mom really had to you
know, pick up the slack.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.530
- It was just the two of us,
up until I left for college.

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:30.950
And that was our family unit.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.440
- My mom was left with four kids,

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.763
a 15-year-old, a 14-year-old,

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.240
an eight-year-old, and a three-year-old.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.840
- I was raised by two very powerful,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.933
very tireless women, tireless mothers,

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.470
for that matter, both
of whom, have not only

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.440
taught me about patience, but about

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.763
the myriad of ways in
which family can manifest.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.780
- My mom was mom and dad for
me for so much of my life.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.660
And I'm just really grateful for it.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.010
- She didn't have a degree.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.880
She didn't have a job of any
kind when she moved out there.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.910
She would just, was
forced to figure it out.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.613
- She was able to get us out
of a very unhealthy marriage.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.500
She did it all on her own.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.560
- It's just now, as an adult,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.510
I'm starting to realize
how strong my mom is.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.520
- She would work, but
she also went to school

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.173
on the weekend, too, and then,

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.140
she worked full time during the week.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.133
- She works six days out of the week,

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:23.383
just to provide for me and my sister.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.000
She never complains.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.940
She has the best sense of humor.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.940
- She started a house cleaning business,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.670
that since its conception, has allowed her

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.500
to provide me with
everything that I've needed

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.103
to have a good start to my life.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.450
- Growing up, I never knew
that anything was wrong.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.580
I always had everything I wanted,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.290
any toy, any game system, all of it,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.110
my mom just got me stuff.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.470
I mean, my mom was the Easter Bunny,

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.453
the Tooth Fairy, Santa, everything.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.523
We never wanted for anything in the world.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:53.690
And then, the older I got, the more

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:55.870
I realized she sacrificed so much.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.193
- She was there every
single sporting outing,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.870
every single choir concert.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.603
No matter how far it was, she was there,

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.950
and she was cheering me on.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.393
- My mom took it upon herself
to teach me how to drive.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.277
And she said, "Mija, if you want to drive,

00:02:10.277 --> 00:02:12.117
"you gotta learn how to change a tire,

00:02:12.117 --> 00:02:14.597
"how to check oil, how
to do all that stuff."

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.207
And I said, "Mom," (clicks
her tongue) I was like,

00:02:16.207 --> 00:02:18.007
"What are you gonna teach
me about doing that?

00:02:18.007 --> 00:02:19.160
"You're a girl."

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.590
And she's like, "Sweetie,
you got it all wrong."

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.140
This lady walked out the house,

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.693
popped the hood to her truck,

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.680
and this lady just starts going at it.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:27.860
- After my dad passed, my mom would

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.620
put us all to bed, and go to her room,

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:30.870
and cry herself to sleep.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.803
- When I was growing up, I
didn't always appreciate,

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.600
let alone, fully
comprehend the real impact

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.940
of the burden that she had to carry

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.810
as primary provider of our household.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.780
- Shout out to all the single moms who are

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.580
pushing forward, and just doing everything

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.480
they can to provide for their kids.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.180
I really, really wish I had understood

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.063
how much my mom was
doing at a younger age,

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.730
so I could have helped
her a little bit more.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.550
- She is the biggest believer in me,

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.020
in this entire world, more so than myself.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.573
She doesn't ever fail to
tell me that she loves me.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.143
- She was always proud of me.
Very proud, I don't know why.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.720
She was always proud of
me, didn't matter for what.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.553
- I don't know.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.593
I don't think single
moms get enough credit,

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.653
because it takes a lot
to be both mom and dad.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.790
You really do give up a lot of yourself

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.153
when you're raising people.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.040
- Mom, Abuelita, I am so gratefully

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.400
indebted to the both of you.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.660
Thank you for all of the love and support.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.853
- I guess all that remains
to be said is thank you, Mom.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.453
I love you a lot.

00:03:27.789 --> 00:03:29.083
- Gracias, Mama.

00:03:29.447 --> 00:03:30.280
Te amo.

